# {{ exercise_title }} — agent guide

**Start at the seam. The rest of the app is yours to change when the seam isn't enough.**

- **The seam** (`exercise/**`) — the per-app code: what students enter, what they see
  afterwards, what the instructions say. Most requests are satisfied here alone, and changes
  here keep this app compatible with every other app in the family.
- **The chassis** (`core/`, `ui/`, `app.py`, `assets/`) — shared machinery. **Editable.** It is
  identical across the family by default, so change it deliberately and run the tests.
- **Deployment state** (`.adalab/app.json`, `project.json`, `card.json`) — the one blocked
  zone. Written by the AdaLab extension, not by hand.

The app is a single-process **Streamlit** application:

```
core/       framework-free Python. Imports streamlit NOWHERE.
            identity, storage, cohorts, results, export, admin, plot helpers.
ui/         thin Streamlit UI — chassis screens.
exercise/   THE SEAM: schema.py, capture.py, analysis.py, content.md.
app.py      entry point, course gate, onboarding, navigation.
```

## Invariants — enforced by tests, not by a hook

Editing the chassis is allowed; breaking these is not. Each has a test that fails.

- **`core/` must never import streamlit.** That is what keeps the UI swappable and makes
  `core/` reusable as a shared library later. `exercise/schema.py` is imported by `core/`, so
  it must stay framework-free too. → `tests/test_core_no_streamlit.py`
- **Never rename `ui/` to `pages/`.** It looks like the Streamlit convention and it is a trap:
  Streamlit switches into magic multipage mode from the directory *name* alone
  (`Path(main_script_parent / "pages").exists()`). Every module in it then becomes a page with
  its own URL and its own sidebar entry — including `login`, `session_url` and `_components`,
  which are machinery, not screens, and which would bypass the course gate in `app.py`. This
  shipped once and confused students. → `tests/test_navigation.py`
- **Plots come from `core.plots`**, which returns `(figure, code_str)` so the chassis can show
  the standalone pandas + plotly in a "Show the code" panel. → `tests/test_show_the_code.py`
- **No per-student data in module-level globals** — Streamlit state is per-session and a
  module global leaks across them. → `tests/test_concurrency.py`
- **`.adalab/` integrity**: container filenames match their `uid`, exactly one primary
  container, no reserved or secret env vars, `stripped_prefix` consistent with Streamlit's
  `--server.baseUrlPath`. → `tests/test_adalab_config.py`

After any chassis change, run the suite:

```
DATA_DIR=$(mktemp -d) python -m pytest -q
```

## Blocked (the hook exits 2)

- `.adalab/app.json`, `.adalab/project.json`, `.adalab/card.json` — deployment state; the
  AdaLab extension owns these and fills in `app_id`, `metadata_id` and
  `current_image_version` at deploy time.
- Commands that would delete the mounted volume, the SQLite database, or `.adalab/`. Student
  results are append-only and have no undo.

## Editable with confirmation

`.adalab/local_container_1.json` (env vars, CPU/RAM, volume mounts) and dependency-add
commands (`pip/uv/poetry install|add`) — a package installed without also landing in
`pyproject.toml` builds locally and then breaks the container.

## You want to… → edit

- Add / change a measurement field → `exercise/schema.py` (storage, CSV and export columns follow)
- Change the input UI → `exercise/capture.py` (returns a payload dict; the chassis validates it)
- Add or change a plot → `exercise/analysis.py`, built with `core.plots` helpers
- Change instructions or the analysis questions → `exercise/content.md`
  (questions are the list items under `## Analysis questions`)
- Change identity, cohorts, storage, exports or the chassis screens → `core/**` and `ui/**`.
  Allowed, but it moves this app away from the family — prefer the seam where it will do, and
  consider whether the change belongs in the template so every app gets it.

## How the pieces fit (so you don't reinvent them)

- **Plots** from `core.plots` come with their reproduction code; the chassis renders it in a
  "Show the code" panel. Hand-building a plotly figure in the seam silently loses that panel,
  which is a teaching requirement (§B7).
- **Identity** is KUID → group → hold → year (§B2). Never add per-student passwords; the
  course password is the gate.
- **Persistence is append-only**: corrections *supersede*, "reset" *closes a year*, nothing is
  deleted. SQLite is the system of record with a long-format CSV mirror; both live on the
  mounted AdaLab Shared Volume at `$DATA_DIR`. The app **fails loud** if that volume is
  missing — never point `DATA_DIR` at a container-local path to "fix" a startup error
  (`STORAGE_MODE=local` is the supported, loudly-flagged alternative).
- **Comparison views are anonymised** (no KUID or group labels) by design.
- **Exports** are produced by `core.export` in all four formats (CSV, Excel, PDF, HTML). Extend
  it rather than building a parallel one.

## Conventions

Style and composition rules are in `.claude/rules/`. Use the **`lab-exercise-app`** skill for
any request to adapt this app, and `/new-exercise-field` to add a measurement field.
